{
 "what": "S2-03 adjudication: the flip claim held its two sides to different evidentiary standards.",
 "verified_by": "MAIN, 2026-08-15, 0 GPU on .73 (zwfy6). Paired item bootstrap, n_boot=10000, seed=7, BOTH acc and the reference recomputed inside every resample. Per-cell results_root taken from heal_readout_v2_permutation_null.json; shard set asserted =={0..7}, n=12032, 0 dup, 0 nan per arm.",
 "the_defect": "vs_null carries ci95/boot_p/exact McNemar for the FLOOR comparison; the CHANCE comparison appears nowhere with any inference attached. So 'above chance but not above the floor' pairs a tested claim with an untested one -- and the untested side is the one that makes the flip look large.",
 "why_the_fix_is_legitimate": "chance = mean_i(1/n_opt_i) is, like the floor, a deterministic function of the evaluated item set, so the paired item bootstrap is exactly the matching test; no new measurement is required.",
 "harness_validation": {
  "floor_side_reproduces_published_v1_delta": "15/15 exact to <1e-6",
  "chance_side_reproduces_papers_count": "10/12 above item-averaged chance by point estimate -- identical to 05_analysis.tex",
  "floor_side_reproduces_papers_count": "1/12 clears the floor -- identical to 05_analysis.tex"
 },
 "counts_12_damaged_non_olmo": {
  "above_chance_point": 10,
  "above_chance_ci": 3,
  "above_floor_point": 3,
  "above_floor_ci": 1,
  "n": 12
 },
 "verdict": "CONFIRMED and material. Under the paper's own asymmetric reporting the flip reads 10/12 above chance vs 1/12 above the floor. Held to a SINGLE standard -- CI excluding zero on both sides -- it reads 3/12 vs 1/12. The flip is real but roughly a third the advertised size, and the 7 cells that lose their 'above chance' label were never above chance by any tested standard. The paper must either test both sides or label both as point estimates; it may not test one and not the other.",
